  "title": "The Listener Sends a Mirror",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "language/communication",
  "premise": "A builder wants to carry out a request, but assumes that make it lighter means use a paler color. Paraphrasing the intended change reveals that the requester meant reduce weight before any work begins.",
  "hook": "Lighter in color, or lighter to carry?",
  "visible_action": "One word forks into a paint swatch and a weighing scale; a confirming reply locks the chosen branch.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Checking meaning can prevent action on an ambiguous request.",
  "gate": "Do not imply confirmation is required for every ordinary low-risk phrase.",
